-- l17NoHull: for N = 2 and f = (0, 1), no phibar satisfies H1, H2a, H2c and H2b, although f >= 0
-- (l17F0Nonneg). Thus the existence needs f k > 0 for k < N (hpos). The induction runs over the prefix p
-- with N fixed: l17Hull N f p phibar is H1 to H2b with the ranges k + 1 < p and D p = 0, and l17Last is
-- the start r of the last segment of phibar. l17HullZero is the base (p = 0). The extension step to
-- t = q + 1 is a Graham scan: l17ArgMax gives the m <= q with the largest slope s from (F m, G m) to
-- (F t, G t). The new phibar is phibar_m below m and s from m (l17ExtA to l17ExtE, with l17Junction
-- at m). l17HullAll is the strong induction, and ironing_exists is the hull at p = N = n + 1.
